<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- A-39b: Liquibase-owned copy of the Spring Batch 6 postgres DDL,
         table-prefixed per service (PSX_BATCH_) for single-writer cleanliness
         (R-34), EXIT_MESSAGE widened to TEXT so CRDB-driver cause chains are
         never truncated.

         LIQUIBASE-SQL-EXCEPTION: this is autogenerated FRAMEWORK DDL owned by
         Spring Batch, not schema this project designs. Hand-transcribing 6 tables
         and 3 sequences into typed tags would fork the framework's own schema and
         make the next Batch upgrade a manual diff, which is the vendor-lock the
         pure-XML rule exists to prevent, not an instance of it. Same precedent as
         PRR 002 and CIX 002.

         Every CREATE carries IF NOT EXISTS, so a pod SIGKILLed mid-migration
         re-runs the file safely; that is ALSO why this changeset carries no
         precondition (A-81: one sqlFile creates nine objects, and a precondition
         sampling one of them reads a half-applied file as complete and skips the
         rest forever). -->
    <changeSet id="psx-002-batch-metadata" author="dcre">
        <!-- A-82: the fleet's copy of this file gained IF NOT EXISTS after it had
             already been applied, changing the enclosing changeset's checksum and
             failing validation on every database that had run it. The escape hatch
             is kept here even though psx-002 has never run anywhere, so a future
             edit to the vendored framework DDL cannot fail validation on a database
             that already has PSX history. It is APPLICABILITY that must stay
             preserved for this file, not the byte-for-byte checksum. -->
        <validCheckSum>ANY</validCheckSum>
        <sqlFile path="db/changelog/2026/08/batch-metadata-psx.sql" splitStatements="true"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
